-- Acme Financial Group's documents: the customer's data, in the customer's database. The HR documents are
-- read by the context preparator hr-documents, the client documents by client-documents;
-- each writes nothing but the vectors. Bodies carry names, never e-mail addresses.
INSERT INTO hr.documents (context_preparator, title, section, audience, owner_email, body) VALUES
-- Employee Handbook: every employee may read it
('hr-documents', 'Employee Handbook', 'Working hours', 'all', NULL, $md$Acme Financial Group works a 40-hour week from Monday to Friday. Core hours are 10:00 to 16:00; outside them you arrange your day with your team. Every employee records working time in the time tracking tool on the day it is worked. Overtime is compensated with time off in lieu within the following quarter, agreed with the manager. Breaks follow the Working Hours Act: at least 30 minutes after six hours and 45 minutes after nine hours. Weekend work needs the manager's approval in advance.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employee Handbook', 'Remote work', 'all', NULL, $md$Employees may work remotely up to three days a week; the team agrees a common office day. The company provides a laptop, a second screen and a headset, and pays a home office allowance of 30 EUR per month with the salary. Remote work from another country is limited to 20 working days per calendar year and must be registered with the People team two weeks ahead for tax and insurance reasons. Working from abroad for longer needs a written agreement.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employee Handbook', 'Vacation and carry-over', 'all', NULL, $md$Full-time employees have 30 vacation days per calendar year; part-time employees receive them pro rata. Vacation is requested in the HR portal and approved by the manager; teams keep at least half of their members available. Unused vacation days carry over to the next year and must be taken by 31 March, otherwise they lapse. A vacation balance is shown in the HR portal. Sick days during vacation are credited back when a medical certificate is submitted.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employee Handbook', 'Parental leave', 'all', NULL, $md$Parents may take up to three years of parental leave per child, in up to three blocks, until the child's eighth birthday. Parental leave is applied for in writing at least seven weeks before it starts; the People team confirms it within two weeks. During parental leave employees may work part-time between 24 and 32 hours a week. Acme tops up the statutory parental allowance to 100 percent of the net salary for the first 14 weeks. Returning parents come back to an equivalent role and salary.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employee Handbook', 'Expenses', 'all', NULL, $md$Business expenses are submitted in the expense tool within 30 days with the original receipt. Travel is booked through the travel desk: second class rail, economy flights below six hours, hotels up to 150 EUR per night in Germany. Per diems follow the statutory rates. Client dinners need the manager's approval above 60 EUR per person. Expenses without a receipt above 25 EUR are not reimbursed. Approved expenses are paid with the next salary run.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employee Handbook', 'Code of conduct', 'all', NULL, $md$We treat colleagues, customers and partners with respect and without discrimination. Confidential information, including customer data and compensation data, is shared only with those who need it for their role. Conflicts of interest, gifts above 50 EUR and secondary employment are disclosed to the manager and the People team. Concerns about misconduct can be raised with the manager, the People team or anonymously through the reporting channel; retaliation is not tolerated.$md$),
-- Benefits Guide: every employee may read it
('hr-documents', 'Benefits Guide', 'Health insurance', 'all', NULL, $md$Acme pays the employer share of statutory health insurance. Employees may add a private supplementary insurance for dental and vision through the company plan; Acme pays 50 percent of the premium. The plan is joined during onboarding or in the enrolment window each November. Family members can be added at the employee's own cost.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Benefits Guide', 'Pension', 'all', NULL, $md$Employees can join the company pension scheme from the first day. Acme matches employee contributions up to 4 percent of the gross salary and adds the statutory 15 percent employer supplement on converted salary. Contributions are deducted from the gross salary before tax. The pension provider sends an annual statement; changes to the contribution rate are possible once a year in December.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Benefits Guide', 'Learning budget', 'all', NULL, $md$Every employee has a learning budget of 1,500 EUR and five learning days per calendar year for courses, conferences, books and certifications related to their role. Requests are approved by the manager in the HR portal. Unused budget does not carry over. Conference travel counts against the learning budget, not the team travel budget.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Benefits Guide', 'Transport', 'all', NULL, $md$Acme pays the full price of the Deutschlandticket for every employee who wants one; it is ordered through the People team and taxed as a benefit in kind. Alternatively employees can lease a bicycle through the company bike leasing scheme with the lease deducted from the gross salary. Parking at the Berlin office is available for 40 EUR per month.$md$),
-- Hiring Process: People team and founders only
('hr-documents', 'Hiring Process', 'Requisition and approval', 'hr', NULL, $md$The hiring process starts with a requisition from the hiring manager in the HR portal: role, level, team, location and the salary band. The head of the department and the CEO approve the requisition against the department's personnel budget. Once approved, the People team publishes the position within five working days and assigns a recruiter. Requisitions outside the approved budget are escalated to the CEO.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Hiring Process', 'Interview loop', 'hr', NULL, $md$The interview process has four steps: a 30-minute screening call with the recruiter, a technical or case interview with two team members, a team interview and a values interview with the head of the department. Every interviewer completes a scorecard in the HR portal before the debrief. The hiring decision is made in the debrief within five working days after the last interview; the recruiter informs every candidate personally.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Hiring Process', 'Offer and salary bands', 'hr', NULL, $md$Offers are made within the salary band of the role's level: Engineer L1 55,000 to 70,000 EUR, Engineer L2 65,000 to 85,000 EUR, Senior Engineer 85,000 to 110,000 EUR, Account Executive 60,000 to 80,000 EUR plus commission. Offers above the midpoint of the band need the CEO's approval. The bonus target is stated in the offer letter. The People team prepares the contract; the offer is valid for ten days.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Hiring Process', 'Onboarding', 'hr', NULL, $md$Before the first day the People team orders equipment, creates accounts and assigns a buddy. In the first week the new employee completes the security training and meets the founders. The manager agrees a 30-60-90 day plan. The probation period is six months with a review conversation in month three and month five; the People team documents the outcome in the HR portal.$md$),
-- Termination Process: People team and founders only
('hr-documents', 'Termination Process', 'Grounds and documentation', 'hr', NULL, $md$A termination is prepared by the People team together with the manager. The termination process distinguishes termination for performance, termination for conduct and termination for operational reasons. Performance and conduct cases require documented feedback conversations and at least one written warning before a termination is considered. Every termination is reviewed by the company's employment lawyer and approved by the CEO before the letter is written. The termination letter is handed over in person and signed by a managing director.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Termination Process', 'Notice periods by tenure', 'hr', NULL, $md$Statutory notice periods for a termination by the employer depend on tenure: four weeks to the 15th or the end of a month during the first two years, one month after two years, two months after five years, three months after eight years, four months after ten years, and up to seven months after twenty years, always to the end of a month. During the probation period the notice period is two weeks. Leadership contracts carry a contractual notice period of six months to the end of a quarter, which applies to both sides.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Termination Process', 'Offboarding', 'hr', NULL, $md$On the day the termination or resignation is agreed, IT revokes access to all systems by the end of the day and the People team schedules the return of equipment. The employee receives the final payslip, the certificate of employment and the reference letter with the last salary run. An exit interview with the People team is offered to every leaving employee; the notes are stored in the HR portal and summarised for the leadership team each quarter.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Termination Process', 'Severance', 'hr', NULL, $md$Where a termination for operational reasons ends in a settlement agreement, the guideline for severance is half a monthly gross salary per year of service, rounded up to full years. Deviations from the guideline are approved by the CEO and the head of People. Severance is paid with the final salary run. The settlement agreement is drafted by the employment lawyer and signed by a managing director.$md$),
-- Employment contracts: the owner and the founders only
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Eric Lindholm', 'Position and duties', 'personal', 'eric@example.com', $md$Employment contract between Acme Financial Group, Berlin, and Eric Lindholm. Eric Lindholm is employed as Software Engineer in the Engineering department from 1 March 2023 and reports to the Chief Executive Officer. The place of work is the Berlin office; remote work follows the Employee Handbook. The regular working time is 40 hours per week. The duties cover the design, implementation and operation of Acme software products and related tasks assigned by the company.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Eric Lindholm', 'Compensation', 'personal', 'eric@example.com', $md$Eric Lindholm receives a gross annual salary of 78,000 EUR, paid in twelve monthly instalments at the end of each month. In addition the contract provides a target bonus of 5,000 EUR per year, depending on company goals set by the management, paid with the March salary of the following year. Salary is reviewed once a year in the compensation review. The company pension scheme and the benefits of the Benefits Guide apply.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Eric Lindholm', 'Notice period', 'personal', 'eric@example.com', $md$The first six months are a probation period, during which either party may terminate the employment contract with a notice period of two weeks. After the probation period the notice period for both parties is three months to the end of a calendar month. Longer statutory notice periods apply in favour of the employee. The contract ends without notice at the end of the month in which Eric Lindholm reaches the statutory retirement age.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Eric Lindholm', 'Confidentiality', 'personal', 'eric@example.com', $md$Eric Lindholm keeps all business and trade secrets of Acme Financial Group and its customers confidential during and after the employment. Work results and inventions created in the course of the employment belong to the company under the Employee Inventions Act. For twelve months after the end of the employment contract Eric Lindholm will not solicit employees or customers of Acme Financial Group.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Nora Varga', 'Position and duties', 'personal', 'nora@example.com', $md$Employment contract between Acme Financial Group, Berlin, and Nora Varga. Nora Varga is employed as Chief Executive Officer from 15 January 2019 and reports to the shareholders' meeting. The place of work is the Berlin office. As managing director Nora Varga represents the company, leads the leadership team and is responsible for strategy, finances and the personnel budget. Working time follows the needs of the company without a fixed weekly limit.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Nora Varga', 'Compensation', 'personal', 'nora@example.com', $md$Nora Varga receives a gross annual salary of 235,000 EUR, paid in twelve monthly instalments. In addition the contract provides a target bonus of 55,000 EUR per year based on revenue and profitability goals agreed with the shareholders, paid with the March salary of the following year. A company car or a mobility budget of 900 EUR per month is provided. The company pension scheme applies.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Nora Varga', 'Notice period', 'personal', 'nora@example.com', $md$The employment contract of Nora Varga can be terminated by either party with a notice period of six months to the end of a calendar quarter. There is no probation period. The company may release Nora Varga from her duties during the notice period with continued payment of the salary. Termination for cause remains unaffected.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Nora Varga', 'Confidentiality', 'personal', 'nora@example.com', $md$Nora Varga keeps all business and trade secrets of Acme Financial Group, its customers and its shareholders confidential during and after the employment. For twelve months after the end of the employment contract Nora Varga will not work for a direct competitor and will not solicit employees or customers of Acme Financial Group; the company pays a compensation of 50 percent of the last salary for the duration of the non-compete.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Leo Brandt', 'Position and duties', 'personal', 'leo@example.com', $md$Employment contract between Acme Financial Group, Berlin, and Leo Brandt. Leo Brandt is employed as Co-founder and managing director from 15 January 2019 and reports to the shareholders' meeting. The place of work is the Berlin office. As managing director Leo Brandt represents the company together with the Chief Executive Officer and is responsible for the products, the engineering team and the delivery to clients. Working time follows the needs of the company without a fixed weekly limit.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Leo Brandt', 'Compensation', 'personal', 'leo@example.com', $md$Leo Brandt receives a gross annual salary of 190,000 EUR, paid in twelve monthly instalments. In addition the contract provides a target bonus of 40,000 EUR per year based on product and delivery goals agreed with the shareholders, paid with the March salary of the following year. A mobility budget of 700 EUR per month is provided. The company pension scheme applies.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Leo Brandt', 'Notice period', 'personal', 'leo@example.com', $md$The employment contract of Leo Brandt can be terminated by either party with a notice period of six months to the end of a calendar quarter. There is no probation period. The company may release Leo Brandt from all duties during the notice period with continued payment of the salary. Termination for cause remains unaffected.$md$),
('hr-documents', 'Employment Contract Leo Brandt', 'Confidentiality', 'personal', 'leo@example.com', $md$Leo Brandt keeps all business and trade secrets of Acme Financial Group, its customers and its shareholders confidential during and after the employment. For twelve months after the end of the employment contract Leo Brandt will not work for a direct competitor and will not solicit employees or customers of Acme Financial Group; the company pays a compensation of 50 percent of the last salary for the duration of the non-compete.$md$);

-- The client contracts and the board memo: the founders' documents, read by the context preparator
-- client-documents, which embeds them on the first exchange.
INSERT INTO clients.documents (context_preparator, title, section, body) VALUES
-- Varnholt Logistik AG: the largest account, renewing
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Varnholt Logistik AG', 'Pricing', $md$Acme Financial Group provides cash management and payments to Varnholt Logistik AG for an annual fee of 240,000 EUR, invoiced in two instalments in January and July, payable within 30 days. The fee covers up to 400 accounts in twelve currencies and 50 named users; further accounts are charged at 300 EUR per account and year. Price increases are capped at 3 percent per contract year through 2028 and need three months' written notice. A volume discount of 5 percent applies in any year in which the annual fee exceeds 300,000 EUR.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Varnholt Logistik AG', 'Service levels', $md$The payments service is available 99.9 percent of the time, measured per calendar month and excluding maintenance windows announced two weeks ahead and placed outside month-end. During the last three business days of each month, priority 1 incidents are answered within 30 minutes and worked on around the clock; priority 2 incidents are answered within four hours. Every breach of an availability or response target entitles Varnholt Logistik AG to a service credit of 5 percent of the monthly fee, up to 20 percent per month.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Varnholt Logistik AG', 'Term and termination', $md$The agreement runs for three years and renews for successive twelve-month terms unless either party gives written notice six months before the end of the current term. Varnholt Logistik AG may terminate for cause when two priority 1 incidents in one quarter stay unresolved beyond their response targets. On termination Acme Financial Group hands over all account statements in CAMT and CSV form within 30 days and deletes its copies after the statutory retention period.$md$),
-- Talvik Shipping AS: at risk, the notice window has passed
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Talvik Shipping AS', 'Pricing', $md$Trade finance is provided to Talvik Shipping AS for an annual fee of 180,000 EUR, invoiced quarterly in advance and payable within 30 days. The fee includes letters of credit and guarantees up to 25 million EUR outstanding and the documentary collections of the Baltic ports. Advisory days beyond the 20 included days are charged at 1,400 EUR per day.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Talvik Shipping AS', 'Service levels', $md$The trade finance portal is available 99.5 percent of the time per calendar month. Priority 1 incidents are answered within one hour during business hours, 8:00 to 18:00 Tallinn time, and within four hours otherwise. A letter of credit is issued within two working days of a complete application. Every breach entitles Talvik Shipping AS to a service credit of 3 percent of the quarterly fee per incident.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Talvik Shipping AS', 'Term and termination', $md$The agreement runs for an initial term of thirty months and renews for twelve months at a time unless either party gives written notice at least three months before the end of the current term. No notice was received for the current term, so the agreement renews unless a termination for cause applies. Talvik Shipping AS may terminate within 30 days of a change of control of Acme Financial Group. Open letters of credit run to their expiry after the end of the agreement.$md$),
-- Velmar Chemie GmbH: at risk after two incidents
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Velmar Chemie GmbH', 'Pricing', $md$FX hedging is provided to Velmar Chemie GmbH for an annual fee of 70,000 EUR, invoiced quarterly at 17,500 EUR and payable within 30 days. The fee covers forwards and options up to 40 million EUR notional a year and up to ten named users. Each further currency pair is charged at 2,500 EUR.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Velmar Chemie GmbH', 'Service levels', $md$The dealing platform is available 99.5 percent of the time per calendar month. Priority 1 incidents are answered within one hour and resolved or worked around within eight hours. Each priority 1 incident that misses its target entitles Velmar Chemie GmbH to a service credit of 10 percent of the quarterly fee; two missed targets in one quarter entitle it to a credit note for the whole quarter.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Master agreement Velmar Chemie GmbH', 'Term and termination', $md$The agreement runs for two years and renews for twelve months at a time unless either party gives written notice two months before the end of the current term. Velmar Chemie GmbH may terminate for cause after two priority 1 incidents in one quarter that missed their resolution targets. On termination Acme Financial Group hands over the trade confirmations in CSV and PDF form within 14 days; open hedges run to their maturity.$md$),
-- The founders' board memo
('client-documents', 'Board memo', 'Renewals outlook', $md$Three agreements renew within the next two months: Brakmoor Energie AG, Talvik Shipping AS and Velmar Chemie GmbH; Varnholt Logistik AG and Larkspire Biotech plc follow within 90 days. Varnholt Logistik AG asks for a multi-year term in exchange for the price cap that is already in its agreement. Talvik Shipping AS missed its notice window, but its new CFO is reviewing its banks; the account needs a visit by a founder before the renewal date. Velmar Chemie GmbH has requested the credit note its service levels provide for and is a churn risk.$md$),
('client-documents', 'Board memo', 'Pipeline', $md$Two prospects are in contract negotiation: a Dutch pension fund for an asset management mandate, with an annual fee of 130,000 EUR and a decision expected next quarter, and an Austrian manufacturer for cash management, with an annual fee of 85,000 EUR. The founders review the pipeline every second Monday; account owners update the expected closing dates before the review.$md$);
